# In 1820, what share of the world could read?
subtitle: "Drag the slice: how many adults could read in 1820? Then watch the world flip in two centuries, and meet the gap between grandparents and grandchildren."
tags: ["history","language","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Could your ancestors read?\" note \"1820\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Gacrux | a mature, wry quiz host; measured but never slow","b":"gemini:Despina | a smooth, sceptical co-host; natural, never exaggerated","take":"lines"}

## In 1820, what share of the world could read?
use: pie_chart
with:
    labels:
      - Can read
      - Can't read
    values:
      - [12, 88]
      - [88, 12]
    stage: 0
    box:
      x: 20
      'y': 160
      w: 620
      h: 500
    label_size: 24
sources:
    - id: owid
      title: Literate and illiterate world population
      authors: Our World in Data, from van Zanden et al. (2014, historical) and UNESCO (recent)
      year: 2025
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/literate-and-illiterate-world-population
      finding: 'share of adults (15+) who can read and write: 12 % in 1820, 21 % in 1900, 81 % in 2000, 88 % in 2024'
    - id: owid_lit
      title: Literacy
      authors: Max Roser and Esteban Ortiz-Ospina, Our World in Data
      year: 2018
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/literacy
      finding: only one in ten people could read and write in 1820; today the share has reversed, with only one in ten illiterate
    - id: gen
      title: Literacy rates of the younger and older population
      authors: Our World in Data, from UNESCO
      year: 2025
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/literacy-rates-of-younger-vs-older-population
      finding: 'India 2024: 97 % of 15–24-year-olds and 46 % of over-65s can read and write'

    icon book size 200 set twemoji x 800 y 520 icon_look picture of "open book" hidden true
    text y1820 "1820" #3d3833 x 800 y 360 font_size 110 hidden true
    text y2024 "today" #3d3833 x 800 y 360 font_size 110 hidden true
    text india "India today" #3d3833 x 500 y 655 font_size 54 hidden true
    icon old size 250 set twemoji x 280 y 410 icon_look picture of "old woman" hidden true
    text old_p "46 %" below old gap 10 #b5482e cites ["gen"] font_size 64 hidden true
    icon kid size 250 set twemoji x 720 y 410 icon_look picture of girl hidden true
    text kid_p "97 %" below kid gap 10 #b5482e cites ["gen"] font_size 64 hidden true
    text old_a "over 65" above old gap 8 #8f887c font_size 40 hidden true
    text kid_a "15–24" above kid gap 8 #8f887c font_size 40 hidden true
    text y1900 "1900: ~1 in 5" #8f887c cites ["owid"] x 800 y 250 font_size 50 hidden true

    card title "In 1820, who could read?"

A: In 1820, what share of the world's adults could read and write? You guess too.
    draw book y1820

    ask "Drag the slice to the share you think could read." on slice_1 store g default "50" keep true
        right: Close: only about twelve percent.
        wrong: Not quite. It was only about twelve percent.

B: About one in eight? But there were books, newspapers, letters!
    highlight slice_1

A: For a lucky few. Even by 190 (@draw y1900@)0, only about one adult in five could read.

    erase y1820 y1900

A: Now jump to today: about eighty-eight percent of adults can read.
    draw y2024

    animate stage 1 duration 3

B: So it flipped. One in eight could read; now one in eight can't.
    highlight slice_2

    erase book y2024 slice_1 slice_2

B: And here's the bit that gets me: you can still see the flip inside one family.
    draw india old kid old_a kid_a

A: In India, ninety-seven percent of people aged fifteen to twenty-four can read, but fewer than half of those over sixty-five.
    draw kid_p old_p

B: So in many homes, the grandchildren read what their grandparents can't.
    highlight old_p kid_p

A: Two centuries of change, in one living room.
    highlight old kid

